    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d332">

                <pb facs="0317" n="309" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg309"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9918: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-06T19:00:00+09:00">September 6, 1937—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 6—6:44 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>351. Our 350, September 6, 1 p.m. Note presented this afternoon to the Foreign
                        Office.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d332-f1"/> The French Ambassador is doing
                    likewise and the British Embassy is still awaiting instructions.<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d332-f2"/></p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai for information of the Commander-in-Chief and for relay to
                    Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d332-f1" n="5" xml:id="d332-f1-content">
                <p>For text, see <ref target="frus1931-41v01#pg_495"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >i</hi>, p. 495</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d332-f2" n="6" xml:id="d332-f2-content">
                <p>The British note was presented September 7.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
